From cd36c33ae1af37a9264ca9604eb55ca1d658e29a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hubert Behaghel <behaghel@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 19:11:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(publishing): preserve terminal newline and configured
 body fonts

Reproduce live append failure at the protected segment end. Open a valid paragraph before terminal insertion and consume the generated trailing newline without deleting the protected one. Exercise Unicode paragraph/list/block appends against a text-request simulator enforcing Docs insertion/deletion boundaries. Apply consumer-configured body text styles to list creation and incremental normal/list edits without changing semantic IR or imposing fonts. Three red-to-green regressions; full strict compilation and 658 SDK tests pass. The selective runtime overlay also passes all 658 tests.
---
